.TH CMP 1
.SH NAME
cmp \- compare two files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "cmp [ \-l ] [ \-s ] file1 file2"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmp
compares two files.
(If
.I file1
is `\-', the standard input is used.)
Under default options,
.B cmp
makes no comment if the files are the same; if they differ, it announces the byte and line number at which the difference occurred.
If one file is an initial subsequence of the other, that fact is noted.
.PP
Options:
.TP 8
.B \-l
Print the byte number (decimal) and the differing bytes (octal) for each difference.
.TP
.B \-s
Print nothing for differing files; return codes only.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compare files
.I a.out
and
.IR prog :
.RS
.nf
cmp a.out prog
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diff(1), comm(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit code 0 is returned for identical files, 1 for different files, and 2 for an inaccessible or missing argument.
.sp
